#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Present the AnduinOS-branded parts of the base system as DecodiumOS.

DecodiumOS keeps receiving the AnduinOS packages it is built on. Their
user-facing files (installer, welcome app, launchers, translations, logos,
the installer slideshow) are diverted with dpkg-divert to *.anduinos and a
DecodiumOS copy is generated in their place. The originals keep receiving
upgrades at the diverted path; an APT hook re-runs this tool after every
dpkg run so the DecodiumOS copies follow them, and re-asserts the DecodiumOS
Plymouth and GDM themes if an AnduinOS package switched them back.

    rebrand            apply (idempotent, only rewrites what changed)
    rebrand --undo     remove every DecodiumOS copy and diversion
    rebrand --check    report what apply would change, change nothing
"""

